Marketing Video Generation Log

  ---                                                                                                            
  Demo Video Generation Prompt
                                                                                                                 
  Format: Screen recording walkthrough, 2–3 minutes, no narration required (on-screen actions speak for
  themselves). Capture at 1440p if possible.                                                                     
                  
  ---                                                                                                            
  Scene 1 — Upload & Evidence Extraction (0:00–0:30)
                                                                                                                 
  Open the app. In the sidebar, confirm patient name, DOB, and clinician are filled. Paste or upload a realistic
  outpatient therapy note that includes:                                                                         
  - A 60-minute session (explicitly stated, e.g. "Session time: 10:00 AM – 11:00 AM")
  - At least 3 timed CPT codes mentioned (e.g. 97110, 97530, 97140)                                              
  - One evaluation code (e.g. 97161)                               
                                                                                                                 
  Click Screen Note. Let the spinner run to completion. Advance to the edit stage.                               
                                                                                                                 
  ---                                                                                                            
  Scene 2 — Auto-Calculated Time Units (0:30–1:10) [Feature 1]                                                   
                                                                                                                 
  Pan to the billing header bar at the top of the edit stage. Highlight two values:
  - Total session minutes (auto-extracted from the note, e.g. "60 min")                                          
  - Max billable units available given that session duration                                                     
                                                                                                                 
  For one timed code (e.g. 97110), type 22 into the Tx Min field. Watch the units badge update live (e.g. → 2    
  units). Then type 7 — show the badge turn red with "0 units (< 8 min)". Type 15 to restore a valid value.      
   
  ▎ If session start/end times were in the note, show the header pulling "10:00 AM – 11:00 AM → 60 min" directly.
                  
  ---                                                                                                            
  Scene 3 — Time Allocation Across Codes (1:10–1:50) [Feature 2]
                                                                                                                 
  With 60 minutes total available, fill in minutes for each timed code one by one:
  - 97110 → 20 min (2 units)                                                                                     
  - 97530 → 22 min (2 units)
  - 97140 → 15 min (1 unit)                                                                                      
                                                                                                                 
  Watch the allocated minutes counter in the billing header update after each entry (e.g. "57 / 60 min used").
  Intentionally over-allocate — type 30 for 97140 — and show the warning state trigger ("exceeds session time"). 
  Correct it back to 15.
                                                                                                                 
  Click Generate Justification on one code. Show the AI draft appear inline, grounded in the note text. Mark the 
  code as reviewed.
                                                                                                                 
  ---             
  Scene 4 — Final Claim Review & Handoff (1:50–2:30) [Feature 3]
                                                                                                                 
  After all codes are reviewed, click Proceed to Review. The stage badge in the sidebar switches to Review.
                                                                                                                 
  Scroll through the confirm page:
  - Each CPT line expanded: code, modifier, units, minutes, diagnosis pointer, justification text                
  - Any compliance warning highlighted in amber                                                                  
  - ICD-10 diagnosis list visible              
                                                                                                                 
  Click Download CMS-1500 Draft — show the .txt file generate. End on the "Submit to Billing Team" button (or the
   download confirmation), leaving it un-clicked to signal human-in-the-loop handoff.                            
                                                                                                                 
