2026-05-06
Issue: When adding a new code with Tx Min value input   
  that makes sense, there is no justification content    
  generated after hitting "Generate". 
  
The empty justification has a different, deeper root cause. Here's the   
  flow:                                                                                   
                                                                                          
  Generate click (app.py)                                                                 
  │                                                                                       
  │  evaluate_single_code(evidence, code, units=N, minutes=M)                             
  │  ← note_text NOT passed → defaults to ""                                              
  │                                                                                       
  ▼                                                                                       
  _run_rag_for_code()                                                                     
  │                                                                                       
  ├─ 1. CPT lookup ──── LOCAL YAML ─────────────────── ✅ always works                    
  │                                                                                       
  ├─ 2. Ingest note to ChromaDB                                                           
  │      condition: patient_id != "unknown-patient" AND note_text non-empty               
  │      patient_id = "unknown-patient" (not passed from app.py)                          
  │      note_text  = ""               (not passed from app.py)                           
  │      → SKIPPED ❌                                                                     
  │                                                                                       
  ├─ 3. retrieve_chunks("unknown-patient", ...)         
  │      → no data exists for this patient → returns [] ❌                                
  │
  ├─ 4. _build_rag_context(chunks=[], cpt_def)                                            
  │      → only CPT definition block, no note sections ❌
  │
  └─ 5. LLM call
         system prompt: "If retrieved context lacks support, set draft_paragraph to null" 
         LLM sees empty Retrieved Chart Sections → returns null ❌
                                                                                          
  app.py: item["justification"] = matched.get("draft_paragraph") or "" → "" (empty)       
                                                                                          
  Root cause: app.py never passes note_text to evaluate_single_code, so the note is never 
  ingested and retrieval always returns [].             
                                                                                          
  Two-part fix:                                         

  1. app.py — pass note_text=st.session_state.note_text (and a stable encounter ID) to    
  rag_evaluate_single_code
  2. _run_rag_for_code — when retrieve_chunks returns [] but note_text is available, fall 
  back to _parse_sections(note_text) (already exists in ingest_patient_docs.py) as        
  pseudo-chunks. This bypasses vector search entirely and always gives the LLM actual note
   content                                                           